  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef dl_vision_transformer(image: list, patch_size: int = 2, embed_dim: int = 4) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Vision Transformer Patch Embedding** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef dl_vision_transformer(image: list, patch_size: int = 2, embed_dim: int = 4) -> list:\n    img = np.array(image, dtype=np.float64)\n    if img.ndim == 2: img = img[np.newaxis, :, :]\n    C, H, W = img.shape; p = int(patch_size)\n    nh, nw = H // p, W // p\n    patches = []\n    for i in range(nh):\n        for j in range(nw):\n            patches.append(img[:, i*p:(i+1)*p, j*p:(j+1)*p].flatten())\n    W_proj = np.ones((C * p * p, int(embed_dim))) * 0.1\n    return np.round(np.dot(np.array(patches), W_proj), 4).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
